cue0032204
01:10:22.720 --> 01:10:28.740
I would like anyone to have questions, please, to step up to the microphone in the middle

cue0032205
01:10:28.740 --> 01:10:33.040
and try to make the question as short and precise as possible.

cue0032206
01:10:33.640 --> 01:10:36.220
With Passover coming, we'll limit it to four questions.

cue0032207
01:10:39.760 --> 01:10:42.900
Professor Fauru, I don't have four questions,

cue0032208
01:10:42.900 --> 01:10:48.580
but I would like to ask for leave to make a comment after the question, if it's possible.

cue0032209
01:10:50.080 --> 01:10:50.900
Go ahead, the question.

cue0032210
01:10:52.720 --> 01:11:02.800
Would you write, please, a book like Maimonides, a modern guide for perplexed?

cue0032211
01:11:02.800 --> 01:11:05.220
They call it in Hebrew, Moreh Nevochim.

cue0032212
01:11:06.300 --> 01:11:07.260
This is my question.

cue0032213
01:11:07.680 --> 01:11:14.000
And how would you apply your doctrine of Jewish ethics and morality to present-day life?

cue0032214
01:11:14.660 --> 01:11:18.040
If you're not ready with an answer, in the meantime, I could make a comment.

cue0032215
01:11:20.940 --> 01:11:22.700
Go ahead. I'm learning. I'm learning.

cue0032216
01:11:22.720 --> 01:11:29.960
The perplexity is here created between our American jurisprudence and reality.

cue0032217
01:11:29.960 --> 01:11:32.880
We are having here a few lawyers.

cue0032218
01:11:32.880 --> 01:11:34.360
I feel it.

cue0032219
01:11:34.360 --> 01:11:37.360
My sixth sense.

cue0032220
01:11:37.360 --> 01:11:38.360
Why?

cue0032221
01:11:38.360 --> 01:11:46.280
We are having a wonderful constitution, a bill of rights, and hundreds of statutes which

cue0032222
01:11:46.280 --> 01:11:48.220
protects our civil rights.

cue0032223
01:11:48.220 --> 01:11:50.920
You name it from A to Z.

cue0032224
01:11:50.920 --> 01:11:56.340
But when you come to a law, to the court of law, you'll face a different story.

cue0032225
01:11:57.080 --> 01:12:03.620
Because with the stroke of a pen, the state judge, a federal judge, even a traffic court judge,

cue0032226
01:12:04.200 --> 01:12:07.260
could cancel out all the laws, including your civil rights.

cue0032227
01:12:07.820 --> 01:12:11.860
Well, it's interesting that in one of the essays by Judge Cardoso,

cue0032228
01:12:11.860 --> 01:12:20.960
published in a book called Law and Literature, Essence on Law and Literature, by Judge Cardoso.

cue0032229
01:12:21.580 --> 01:12:25.980
He points out the need, what he calls a ministry of justice in the United States,

cue0032230
01:12:26.080 --> 01:12:30.380
because sometimes the rendering of decisions has nothing to do with justice.

cue0032231
01:12:30.500 --> 01:12:31.240
It is a problem.

cue0032232
01:12:31.240 --> 01:12:36.480
But in Judaism, really, one of the things that we had was the combination law-ethics

cue0032233
01:12:36.480 --> 01:12:42.300
made the judge accountable on ethical principles.

cue0032234
01:12:42.420 --> 01:12:45.320
That was, I think, is an advantage rather than the total divorce

cue0032235
01:12:45.320 --> 01:12:48.860
that we have in Western tradition between law and ethics.

cue0032236
01:12:50.320 --> 01:12:51.120
Go ahead.

cue0032237
01:12:53.080 --> 01:12:54.380
Regarding the law,

cue0032238
01:12:55.760 --> 01:12:56.980
I for an I,

cue0032239
01:12:58.040 --> 01:12:59.100
it seems to me,

cue0032240
01:13:00.540 --> 01:13:03.280
this is not one time mentioned in the Tora,

cue0032241
01:13:03.280 --> 01:13:08.000
that one statement says

cue0032242
01:13:08.000 --> 01:13:11.580
what he is doing to his fellow man

cue0032243
01:13:11.580 --> 01:13:14.020
the same thing shall be done to him.

cue0032244
01:13:14.780 --> 01:13:18.040
